<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.15.4: The Graph of a Function in Vertex Form</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02015</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.15.4: The Graph of a Function in Vertex Form</md:title>
    <md:uuid>68aab0c2-db09-4181-b909-dd9b00be5aa2</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
    <section id="sect-00002">
<title>Launch</title>
<para id="para-00001">Since this activity was designed to be completed without technology, ask students to put away any devices.</para>
<para id="para-00002">Answer questions 1 – 3 about the function \(f\), given by \(f(x)=(x+3)^2−1\).</para></section>
<section id="sect-00003"><title>Student Activity</title>
  <exercise id="fdeab50c-b8e2-4440-b2c6-db723a810af4" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00001"><para id="para-00003">What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph of \(f\)?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00001"><para id="para-00004">Correct! -3</para><para id="para-00005">The correct answer is -3.</para></solution></exercise>
      
  <exercise id="_7e781736-842e-456a-bb60-65431c204ede" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00002"><para id="para-00006">What is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph of \(f\)?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00002"><para id="para-00007">Correct! -3</para><para id="para-00008">The correct answer is -3.</para></solution></exercise>
      
  <exercise id="_9b46c74b-35c7-4669-a791-76fa42b078a3" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00003"><para id="para-00009">Does the graph open up or down?</para>
      </problem>
      <solution id="sol-00003"><para id="para-00010">Correct! The graph opens upward. The squared term has a positive coefficient \((1)\).</para><para id="para-00011">Incorrect. The correct answer is Up. The graph opens upward. The squared term has a positive coefficient \((1)\).</para></solution></exercise>
    </section></section>
</content></document>